ARTICLE 5 — COMMERCIAL USE AUTHORIZATION
===============================================================================

5.1 Commercial Use Requires Prior Written Authorization. Notwithstanding any
    other provision of this License, you may NOT use the Software or any
    Derivative Work for any Commercial Use unless and until you have obtained
    a valid, written Commercial Authorization from the Licensor that
    specifically covers such Commercial Use. Any Commercial Use undertaken
    without a valid Commercial Authorization constitutes a material breach of
    this License and an infringement of the Licensor's intellectual property
    rights.

5.2 Application Process. To apply for a Commercial Authorization, you must
    submit a written application to the Licensor at the contact address
    specified in Appendix A. Your application must include, at a minimum:
    (a) the legal name, registration number (e.g., unified social credit code
        or equivalent), principal place of business, and contact information
        of the applicant;
    (b) the names and contact information of any Affiliates that will use the
        Software under the Commercial Authorization, if applicable;
    (c) the specific version(s) of the Software you intend to use;
    (d) a detailed description of the intended Commercial Use, including
        whether it involves internal use, redistribution, SaaS/PaaS hosting,
        embedding in hardware, or any other form;
    (e) the intended business scenario, target market, and estimated user
        scale and deployment scale;
    (f) whether you intend to distribute any Derivative Work in closed-source
        or proprietary form, and if so, the proposed distribution model;
    (g) a description of the data types and volumes expected to be processed
        through the Software, including whether any personal data or sensitive
        personal data will be processed;
    (h) a description of the security measures you have implemented or will
        implement to protect the Software and User Data;
    (i) any other information reasonably requested by the Licensor.

    A template for the Commercial Authorization application is provided in
    Appendix B.

5.3 Evaluation and Grant. The Licensor shall use reasonable endeavors to
    respond to a complete application within thirty (30) business days of
    receipt. The Licensor reserves the right, in its sole and absolute
    discretion, to grant or deny any application for Commercial Authorization,
    and to impose such terms and conditions as it deems appropriate, including
    but not limited to:
    (a) authorization fees, royalties, or revenue-sharing arrangements;
    (b) attribution and branding requirements;
    (c) quality, security, data protection, and compliance standards;
    (d) geographic, field-of-use, or temporal limitations;
    (e) reporting and audit obligations;
    (f) requirements to contribute improvements or bug fixes back to the
        Software community;
    (g) requirements to maintain adequate insurance;
    (h) requirements to comply with applicable laws and regulations, including
        data protection laws, AI regulations, and export control laws.

5.4 Scope of Commercial Authorization. A Commercial Authorization is personal
    to the named licensee and applies only to the specific Commercial Use,
    version(s), scope, and term described in the Commercial Authorization. You
    must use the Software strictly in accordance with the terms of the
    Commercial Authorization. In the event of any conflict between the
    Commercial Authorization and this License, the Commercial Authorization
    shall prevail solely within the scope expressly granted therein; all
    matters not expressly addressed by the Commercial Authorization remain
    governed by this License.

5.5 Non-Transferability. A Commercial Authorization may not be assigned,
    sublicensed, or otherwise transferred to any third party without the
    prior written consent of the Licensor. Any purported assignment or
    transfer in violation of this Section 5.5 shall be null and void ab
    initio.

5.6 Non-Commercial Use Exempt. Non-Commercial Use of the Software, as defined
    in Section 1.4, does not require a Commercial Authorization, but remains
    subject to all other terms and conditions of this License.

5.7 No Implied Authorization. No course of dealing, delay, or failure by the
    Licensor to enforce any provision of this License shall be construed as a
    Commercial Authorization or as a waiver of the Licensor's right to require
    Commercial Authorization for any Commercial Use.

5.8 Material Change Notification. If you hold a valid Commercial Authorization
    and there is any material change in your use of the Software (including
    but not limited to a change in the nature or scope of Commercial Use, a
    change in control of your entity, or a material expansion of deployment
    scale), you must notify the Licensor in writing within fifteen (15)
    business days of such change. The Licensor may require you to enter into
    an amended Commercial Authorization to cover such changed use.

5.9 Records. If you hold a valid Commercial Authorization, you must maintain
    accurate records of your use of the Software and its Derivative Works for
    a period of at least three (3) years following the expiration or
    termination of the Commercial Authorization, and you must make such records
    available to the Licensor upon reasonable request for audit purposes.

