ARTICLE 6 — DATA PRIVACY AND SECURITY
===============================================================================

6.1 Data Controller Responsibility. If you use the Software or its Derivative
    Works to process User Data, you are solely responsible for:
    (a) determining the legal basis for processing such User Data;
    (b) complying with all applicable data protection and privacy laws and
        regulations, including but not limited to the Personal Information
        Protection Law of the People's Republic of China (PIPL), the General
        Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) (EU) 2016/679, the California
        Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), and any other applicable data protection
        laws;
    (c) providing all required notices to data subjects and obtaining any
        required consents;
    (d) implementing appropriate technical and organizational measures to
        protect User Data from unauthorized access, use, disclosure,
        alteration, or destruction.

6.2 No Data Collection by Licensor. The Licensor does not collect, store, or
    process any User Data through the Software. The Software is designed to
    run locally on your own infrastructure, and the Licensor has no access to
    User Data processed through the Software. You acknowledge and agree that
    the Licensor is not a data processor or data controller with respect to any
    User Data processed through the Software.

6.3 Data Localization and Cross-Border Transfer. If you transfer User Data
    across national borders, you are solely responsible for complying with all
    applicable cross-border data transfer laws and regulations, including but
    not limited to the cross-border data transfer requirements under PIPL and
    GDPR. The Licensor makes no representation or warranty regarding the
    permissibility of any cross-border data transfer.

6.4 Security Incident Notification. If you become aware of or reasonably
    suspect a Security Incident affecting the Software or User Data processed
    through the Software, you must:
    (a) take immediate remedial action to contain and mitigate the Security
        Incident;
    (b) notify the Licensor in writing within seventy-two (72) hours of
        becoming aware of or reasonably suspecting the Security Incident,
        unless applicable law requires a shorter notification period;
    (c) provide the Licensor with all information reasonably necessary to
        assess the scope and impact of the Security Incident;
    (d) cooperate with the Licensor in any investigation or remediation
        efforts.

    This notification obligation applies regardless of whether the Security
    Incident is your fault or the fault of any third party.

6.5 Security Measures for Commercial Users. If you hold a valid Commercial
    Authorization, you must implement and maintain reasonable and appropriate
    security measures to protect the Software and User Data, including but not
    limited to:
    (a) access controls and authentication mechanisms;
    (b) encryption of User Data at rest and in transit;
    (c) regular security assessments and vulnerability scanning;
    (d) secure software development practices for any Derivative Works;
    (e) logging and monitoring of access to and use of the Software;
    (f) incident response and disaster recovery procedures;
    (g) personnel security and training measures.

6.6 Data Deletion. Upon termination of this License or any Commercial
    Authorization, you must, upon request of the Licensor or as required by
    applicable law, delete or anonymize all User Data processed through the
    Software in your possession or control, and certify such deletion in
    writing upon request.

6.7 Subprocessor Management. If you engage any third party to process User
    Data on your behalf in connection with the Software, you must ensure that
    such third party is bound by data protection obligations no less protective
    than those set forth in this Article 6, and you remain fully liable for
    any acts or omissions of such third party.

