ARTICLE 7 — RESPONSIBLE AI USE AND PROHIBITED USES
===============================================================================

7.1 Responsible Use Obligation. You agree to use the Software and its
    Derivative Works in a responsible manner that complies with all applicable
    laws, regulations, and ethical standards. You are solely responsible for
    any content, outputs, or actions generated through or by the Software, and
    for ensuring that such content, outputs, or actions do not violate
    applicable law or the rights of any third party.

7.2 Prohibited Uses. You may NOT use the Software or its Derivative Works for
    any Prohibited Use, including but not limited to the uses set forth in
    Appendix C (Prohibited Uses List). The Prohibited Uses List in Appendix C
    is illustrative and non-exhaustive; the Licensor may update the Prohibited
    Uses List from time to time by posting an updated version in the
    Software's official repository, and any such update shall apply to your use
    of the Software from the date of posting.

7.3 AI Safety and Compliance. If you use the Software or its Derivative Works
    to deploy, operate, or provide access to any AI model or AI system, you
    must:
    (a) comply with all applicable AI laws and regulations, including but not
        limited to the Interim Measures for the Management of Generative
        Artificial Intelligence Services (China), the EU AI Act (Regulation
        (EU) 2024/1689), and any other applicable AI regulations;
    (b) implement appropriate content moderation and safety filtering mechanisms
        for any AI outputs generated through the Software;
    (c) provide clear and conspicuous disclosures to end users when content,
        decisions, or actions are generated by AI;
    (d) implement human oversight for any AI system that makes decisions with
        material real-world effects, including but not limited to financial
        transactions, contract execution, employment decisions, legal
        decisions, healthcare decisions, and access to essential services;
    (e) maintain records of AI system deployments and make such records
        available to regulatory authorities upon request, as required by
        applicable law.

7.4 No Circumvention of Safety Features. You may not, and may not permit any
    third party to, circumvent, disable, remove, or interfere with any safety
    features, content filters, or access controls implemented in the Software
    or any AI model accessed through the Software. You may not attempt to
    jailbreak, prompt-inject, or otherwise manipulate any AI model to produce
    harmful, illegal, or prohibited content.

7.5 High-Risk AI Systems. If you use the Software or its Derivative Works to
    deploy any AI system that is classified as "high-risk" under any
    applicable AI regulation (including but not limited to the EU AI Act), you
    must comply with all additional obligations applicable to high-risk AI
    systems, including but not limited to risk assessment, data governance,
    technical documentation, record-keeping, transparency, human oversight,
    accuracy, robustness, cybersecurity, and conformity assessment obligations.

7.6 Liability for AI Outputs. You acknowledge and agree that the Licensor is
    not responsible for any content, outputs, decisions, or actions generated
    through or by the Software or any AI model accessed through the Software.
    You are solely liable for any harm, loss, or damage arising from such
    content, outputs, decisions, or actions, including but not limited to
    claims for defamation, copyright infringement, privacy violations, or
    personal injury.

