ARTICLE 10 — SECURITY VULNERABILITY DISCLOSURE
===============================================================================

10.1 Safe Harbor for Good-Faith Security Researchers. The Licensor hereby
     affirms that it will not initiate or threaten any legal action against
     any person who, in good faith, discovers, reports, or assists in the
     remediation of a security vulnerability in the Software, provided that
     such person:
     (a) acts in good faith and with the intent to improve the security of the
         Software;
     (b) does not access, use, or disclose any User Data, personal data, or
         proprietary information of the Licensor or any third party, except as
         reasonably necessary to demonstrate the vulnerability;
     (c) does not modify, alter, or damage the Software or any system on
         which the Software is deployed, except as reasonably necessary to
         demonstrate the vulnerability;
     (d) does not deny service to any user or disrupt the operation of the
         Software;
     (e) promptly reports the vulnerability to the Licensor in accordance with
         the process set forth in Appendix D;
     (f) allows the Licensor a reasonable period of time to remediate the
         vulnerability before disclosing it publicly (coordinated disclosure);
     (g) does not exploit the vulnerability for any purpose other than
         demonstrating its existence to the Licensor.

10.2 Vulnerability Reporting Process. Security vulnerabilities should be
     reported to the Licensor in accordance with the Security Vulnerability
     Reporting Policy set forth in Appendix D. The Licensor acknowledges
     receipt of all vulnerability reports and uses reasonable endeavors to
     respond to valid reports within a reasonable timeframe.

10.3 Coordinated Disclosure Timeline. The Licensor requests that security
     researchers allow a minimum of ninety (90) days from the date of
     reporting a vulnerability before disclosing it publicly, unless the
     Licensor agrees in writing to a shorter disclosure period. The Licensor
     may request an extension of the disclosure period if additional time is
     needed to remediate the vulnerability, and the Licensor will keep the
     researcher informed of the remediation progress.

10.4 No Waiver of Rights. Nothing in this Article 10 shall be construed as a
     waiver of any right or remedy available to the Licensor against any
     person who does not act in good faith or who violates any provision of
     this Article 10 or applicable law. The safe harbor in Section 10.1
     applies only to acts undertaken in compliance with this Article 10.

10.5 Bug Bounty. The Licensor may, from time to time, operate a bug bounty
     program that provides rewards for valid vulnerability reports. The terms
     and conditions of any such bug bounty program shall be published in the
     Software's official repository. In the event of any conflict between a
     bug bounty program and this Article 10, the bug bounty program terms
     shall prevail solely with respect to the specific rewards and procedures
     set forth in the bug bounty program.

